      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u help me with something? we're updating our internal handbook and i need a quick summary of what we actually have to do when someone submits a 'right to be forgotten' request under gdpr. just like a step-by-step of the process so i can give it to the dev team. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under the GDPR, a 'right to erasure' (or 'right to be forgotten') request requires you to follow a specific process. Here's a step-by-step guide:\n\n1. Receive a request: Acknowledge the request from the individual.\n2. Verify the request: Check if the request is legitimate and if you have processed the individual's data.\n3. Collect information: Gather all relevant information about the data, including its storage, processing, and retention.\n4. Determine => erasure or partial erasure: Decide whether to erase the data entirely or partially, based on the purpose of the processing.\n5. Provide notification: Inform the individual of the decision made, stating whether erasure has been made, transferred to another controller, or would be carried out in the future.\n6. Update records: Document the response and make necessary changes to your records and systems.\n7. Rectification or erasure (if applicable): Carry out the agreed-upon action, which may include deleting or blocking the data.\n\nThis process typically takes 30 days for response, and you should also consider data protection laws in other countries if applicable.",
